Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='train', at=datetime(2026, 10, 3, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The merge queue is scripts/train.sh; reviewed PRs ride a train and nobody merges a train by hand', body='*The merge queue is `scripts/train.sh`* (2026-10-03; GitHub\'s is for organisations, and the gate is the box\'s): reviewed PRs ride a TRAIN. `build <pr>...` merges them onto `train` from `origin/master` in an order that is a function of their heads (2026-10-19): a PR whose head holds more of the others\' merges first, so a stacked PR\'s merge carries its base (`in`, its `Completes:` on that merge once, named in `Carries:`), and the head\'s name orders the rest; "Merge \\#N: \\<title>" with the PR\'s URL. A `refs/pull/<n>/head` behind the head GitHub names refuses the build; a changelog conflict of additions is joined, a line a PR wrote under Unreleased that its merge put under a release is moved back, and `app/Cargo.lock` keeps the train\'s side and cargo adds the PR\'s; any other conflict is skipped for its author. `gate` runs only inside `.#triage`, refusing a variable its steps read that the caller exported and the shell does not set (`SUZATARY_SHELL_SETS`), runs each half here in a worktree of its own at the train\'s commit (`.git/train/worktree`, cargo\'s target moved in and back out), so the checkout can change under it, and keeps each verdict in `.git/train/`, keyed by half and tree (a tree both green and red is a flaky gate, and lands nothing); `gate --remote <codespace>` runs the tree half in that Codespace over `gh codespace ssh` (each commit sent as a git bundle down the pipe, so the Codespace holds no credential; the gate run detached there and its log read once a minute, so a dropped connection costs a poll; the Codespace stopped as soon as its half is done, its keep-alive ending with the train; `scripts/gate-codespace.sh` makes it, idle timeout 10 minutes) while the live half runs here; `gate --remote github` runs it in core instead (2026-10-20, docs/OPERATOR.md): the steps that read this repository on the box, then the train commit\'s public tree, once its leak guard passes, pushed to core\'s `gate/<train sha>` alone, where `.github/workflows/gate.yml` runs the other lanes in parallel on free arm runners; a job\'s gate exiting 1 is red, success green, anything the runners did no verdict; `bisect` finds the merge that turned a red half red; `land` pushes master only from a HEAD both halves passed, then publishes it, then `scripts/deploy.sh <rev>` is the operator\'s. A STACKED PR branches from its base PR\'s branch and lands with it or after it, in the same train or a later one. Nobody merges a train by hand.', rationale="Decided 2026-10-03: GitHub's merge queue is for organisations, and the gate is the box's. The merge order follows the heads since 2026-10-19; gate --remote github since 2026-10-20.", supersedes=()))